NsinfoTradButton = Translate from my language (%s)
NsinfoTradShort = Translate
NsinfoTradDone = Text translated: save it with Update
NsinfoTradCondDeepl = <ul><li><b>Free</b> plan: 500,000 characters per month at no cost; once the quota is reached, translation is refused until the next month. <b>Pro</b> plan: billed on usage.</li><li>The service uses the host <code>api-free.deepl.com</code> (Free) or <code>api.deepl.com</code> (Pro): the plan chosen must match the key.</li><li>HTML tags are kept.</li><li>An API key is obtained in the DeepL API account (check the exact form of a Free key in your account).</li></ul>
NsinfoTradCondGoogle = <ul><li>Cloud Translation Basic (v2): 500,000 characters per month free, then about $20 per million characters (check Google's pricing page).</li><li>A Google Cloud project with billing enabled is required, even for the free quota.</li><li>Authentication by API key; the Cloud Translation API must be enabled in the project.</li><li>HTML tags are kept.</li></ul>
NsinfoTradCondAzure = <ul><li><b>F0</b> free tier: 2 million characters per month; beyond that, pay-as-you-go (about $10 per million, third-party source to check).</li><li>An Azure subscription and a <i>Translator</i> resource are required; key and region come from the Azure Portal.</li><li>Document translation is not included in the free tier (not used here).</li><li>HTML tags are kept.</li></ul>
NsinfoTradCondLibretranslate = <ul><li>Hosted service <code>libretranslate.com</code>: paid API key (about $9 per month, 80 requests per minute) for production use.</li><li><b>Free if you host it yourself</b> (Docker or pip): enter the URL of your server; the key is optional depending on its setup.</li><li>Third-party public instances exist but can change or require a key.</li><li>HTML tags are kept.</li></ul>
NsinfoTradCondMymemory = <ul><li>Free, no key: about 5,000 characters per day anonymously, about 50,000 with an email address (the unit, characters or words, is to check on the MyMemory limits page).</li><li>500 bytes maximum per request: the module cuts the text automatically.</li><li>Plain text only: HTML tags are removed before translation.</li><li>Translation memory plus machine translation: quality varies.</li></ul>
NsinfoTradCondLingva = <ul><li>Free, no key or account.</li><li>Open front end querying Google Translate without an official API: operation is not guaranteed.</li><li>Public instances (for example lingva.ml) are run by volunteers and can be unavailable or limited: prefer your own instance.</li><li>Plain text only: HTML tags are removed before translation.</li></ul>
